Azure Monitor Workbooks provide interactive reports and visualizations that combine Azure monitoring data into a single, customizable interface. Workbooks can bring together metrics, logs, text, charts, and other visual elements to create operational dashboards.

Common uses include:

* Application performance monitoring
* Infrastructure health reporting
* Security monitoring
* Capacity analysis
* Incident investigation
* Executive reporting

For example, an operations team can create a workbook showing virtual machine CPU utilization, network traffic, storage performance, active alerts, and application availability in one place.

A real-life use case is a Network Operations Center monitoring hundreds of Azure resources through standardized operational workbooks.

Workbooks make complex monitoring information easier to understand and help administrators identify trends and operational issues.
